.TH OROC-RUN 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.3" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-run \- Run application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc run [options] [<project\-or\-source>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run application. Provide a project directory, HTML file, or JavaScript module. When no oro.toml is found, oroc infers a minimal configuration automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-headless\fR
run application in headless mode (without frame or window)
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<platform>\fR
platform target to run application on (defaults to host):
.br
\(bu android
.br
\(bu android\-emulator
.br
\(bu ios
.br
\(bu ios\-simulator
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml/oro.ini file
.TP
\fB\-\-port=<port>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific port (if host is not specified, defaults to localhost)
.TP
\fB\-\-host=<host>\fR
load "index.html" from a specific host (if port is not specified, defaults to 80)
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
build for production (disables debugging info, inspector, etc.)
.TP
\fB\-\-test[=path]\fR
indicate test mode, optionally importing a test file relative to resource files
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-debug\fR
enable debug mode
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
hint for less log output
.TP
\fB\-E, \-\-env\fR
add environment variables
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR
allow external command execution (gates ndk\-build/gradle/git/build scripts)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-keylog=<path>\fR
write NSS TLS key log lines to <path> (OpenSSL provider)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBORO_DEBUG\fR
enable debug mode (like \-D)
.TP
\fBORO_VERBOSE\fR
enable verbose logs (like \-V)
.SH COMMON ERRORS
.PP
For CI/Linux headless, install `xvfb\-run` or set a custom headless runner in your config. Use `\-\-test=path` to run tests bundled with your app.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc run .\fR
build and launch the current project on the host platform
.TP
\fBoroc run \-\-platform=android\-emulator .\fR
build and launch the current project on the Android emulator target
.TP
\fBoroc run \-\-headless \-\-test=tests/smoke.js .\fR
execute a bundled test entrypoint in headless mode
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
